Package: OmicOne
Title: Interactive Local Multi-Omics Analysis Studio
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R:
    person("OmicOne", "Authors", email = "noreply@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A localhost-first, browser-based interactive application for
    multi-omics analysis. Users launch the app with a single command, pick an
    omics type, and work through that pipeline step by step -- entirely on their
    own machine, with no cloud server. The single-cell RNA-seq pipeline is
    complete: twenty-one steps from import and quality control through doublet
    removal, normalization, dimensionality reduction, batch integration,
    clustering, embedding, markers, annotation, enrichment, trajectory, RNA
    velocity, cell-cycle and signature scoring, cell-cell communication, CNV /
    malignancy inference, survival analysis, visualization, a narrated report
    and export. The whole-exome / somatic mutation pipeline is complete too:
    twelve steps over maftools, from MAF import through the cohort summary,
    oncoplot, mutation spectra, tumour mutational burden, lollipop plots,
    driver detection, mutational signatures, clinical and pathway enrichment,
    cohort comparison, mutation-survival and heterogeneity. Bulk RNA-seq,
    spatial transcriptomics and multi-omics integration are on the roadmap and
    show their planned steps in the interface. Every step offers method
    alternatives, adjustable thresholds, a beginner-friendly explanation, a
    result summary, a large preview plot, and reproducible parameter logging.
